he motive at all. In this case, though, what have we learned about the shooter here?\par \par \uc2 BEN COLLINS, NBC NEWS SENIOR REPORTER: That`s true. So, with the Colorado shooter, we have learned several things. First of all, they have -- we`ve traced down I have an online account tied to him, which is very hard. There is not much under his actual name. That`s in part because he changed his name a few years ago to an entirely different name to separate his original name from his father.\par \par \uc2 They reached out to his father earlier today, a bunch of media networks, and they asked him about the shooting. And he said he had talked to attorneys, and the attorneys told him he had shot up a gay bar. And the father said, I asked if he was gay, and they said no. And he said -- and the father said few, as in like few. He`s not gay.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 COLLINS: That`s the sort of lifestyle he was living in. But the larger thing that we learn about his online identity was he was in an interesting feud I would say with a hate site called Encyclopedia Dramatica. That site has been tied to two different mass killings. One is a guy named William Atchison back from 2017. He`s shot up a school in New Mexico, killed two people. He was a sysop or an admin at that website.\par \par \uc2 What`s notable about this website specifically is that it has a kill count for mass shooters. And it`s almost like a high-score thing. There`s actually a section of the site called high scores. And if you target gay people or minorities, they note that with slurs in the profile. And they have updated his profile to note that as well.\par \par \uc2 Also, because of this, he was -- I just want to note this really quick -- really quickly, Chris. Because of this, he was mercilessly bullied and he tried to bully back the same people on this website for years. And he was living with his grandmother. And at one point, according to local news there, there was -- there`s some leaked