m -- and we can confirm this too, that his mom referred to him as he on the day of the shooting, both in text messages and on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So, it`s possible -- and that`s certainly the narrative that is running through the far-right internet, that this was somehow not tied to homophobia in any way, but the five hate crimes charges kind of run in the face of that.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Yes. Again, I think it`s probably the darkest thing possible. I think the remembrances that we`ve seen for the survivors and for those who died have been remarkable. The way that community has come together has been remarkable. And I think, in some ways, the \uc2 Walmart\uc2  shooting just three days later illustrates how guns end up being the throughline no matter where the darkness comes from in its origination.\par \par \uc2 Ben Collins, thank you very much. I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 COLLINS: Thanks, Chris.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Still to come, Georgia Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  could be among the worst major candidates in recent history. Now, a new report says he may not even live in Georgia at all, or at least not like his primary residence. That`s ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [20:40:00]\par \par \uc2 HAYES: This week, we have a fascinating new episode on my podcast Why Is This Happening? where I got a chance to talk to a former currency trader turns soldier who`s currently right now fighting in Ukraine. He`s a British man who goes by the pseudonym Macer Gifford. He fought against ISIS in Syria from 2015 to 2017, arrived in Ukraine just 10 days before the Russian invasion. And he explained how actual combat quickly separates out the adventure seekers from those who are truly invested in the cause.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACER GIFFORD, VOLUNTEER SOLDIER IN UKRAINE: I`ve been hit by suicide bombs. I`ve been shot myself. I`ve been blown up. Just about everything has happened to me. And believe me,