at, can you give us a sense of the get out the vote effort? Harry Reid is no longer there. He played such a pivotal role in organizing the vote effort in the state of Nevada. The culinary workers union is Democratic, how effective do you think their efforts were? Is it meaningful to the average culinary worker is a 44 -year-old Latina at a moment where we`re talking about such a pocketbook issues.\par \par \uc2 [21:25:02]\par \par \uc2 We`re talking about economic issues.\par \par \uc2 Do you think that helps the Democrats message going into the elections?\par \par \uc2 RALSTON: Well, that`s a great question, Alex, and a very relevant question. As Rachel mentioned, there were about 60,000 ballots that were taken from this drop boxes that were put in there yesterday. Guess which union ran a drop box campaign with its members to try to help \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  and the Democratic ticket?\par \par \uc2 That`s right, the culinary union. It`s interesting that you mentioned the profile of the Latino worker for the culinary. It`s such an integral cog in the machine, they are the Hispanic turnout machine and in Nevada. And for that turn out with that 44-year-old Latina, the first Latina ever elected to the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 , has been a motivating factor for the union members.\par \par \uc2 And so, I think the Democrats hope that the huge proportion of the 60,000 ballots that came in yesterday into this but drop boxes were culinary driven, and therefore we`re really helping the Democratic ticket up and down.\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: Jon, I know that prognosticating should not be something that any of us do without talking through the data. But as an election observer in Nevada, you can feel the currents here better than anybody else that I know, which is why you and I have been talking about Nevada elections for so long now. Do you feel at the end of the day that the Democrats have a shot at the senator`s race, at the Senate race, at the governor`s race?\par \pa