ellwether for Democrats. I mean, I spent time with her in 2018. I mean, she is the -- she is the canary in the coal mine and a lot of ways, literally, every election cycle.\par \par \uc2 [22:30:00]\par \par \uc2 She`s a great candidate, great campaigner, and I`m sure we`re going to be reading more.\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: We have a changing characterization in an important Senate race. The Ohio Senate race this has previously been characterized by NBC News as too early to call. It is still too early to call but NBC News now says the Republican candidate J.D. Vance is leading in this Ohio Senate race.\par \par \uc2 We`re going to be getting more information about that. We`re also going to be taking a quick break right now because when we come back we`re going to be getting oh -- sorry we have another call.\par \par \uc2 I hereby interrupt my thought to tell you that there is a projection in the Pennsylvania governor`s race. Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  is the projected winner against Republican candidate \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 . Wow. In Pennsylvania, again, it is -- we do not have a characterization of a winner let alone a leader even in the Senate race.\par \par \uc2 But in this governor`s race, NBC News has projected the winner. \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  versus \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  was one of the starkest -- well, I mean will say it, the Wisconsin races, the governor`s race and the Senate race in Wisconsin a very, very stark contrasts between those candidates but the Pennsylvania governor`s race with \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  and \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , it was harder to get two candidates who offered different visions for the state that were more different than the two of them.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: The governor`s race and the secretary of state race because the governor appoint the secretary of state and what is going to happen in Pennsylvania with Mastriano was one of those issues, one of those possibilities that made \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  say democracy is on 