ection, people are ready to get back to normalcy, there`s an exhaustive majority out there, Democrats Republicans and independents, and they just want to push out the extremists.\par \par \uc2 Like they don`t want to vote for people who think that the election was stolen. They don`t want to vote for people who want to ban books, they don`t want to vote for people who want to national abortion ban, or like JD Vance says, where women of how marriage should say in that marriage for the sake of her kids, like that`s insanity. And Ohio could be conservatives, but Ohio isn`t crazy. We`re not going to go down this road. We don`t want to run around, we don`t want our senator hanging out with \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 . We don`t want that.\par \par \uc2 And I`m telling, you that we are going to win this race. J.D. Vance is going to get put to bed, he`s going to end up back in California, and are going to try to help this country move into an age of possibility, and major reform, in an age of reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 That`s why I`m running. We had take the temperature down, push off the extremists, and getting back to being Americans.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: When J.D. Vance was a Republican venture capitalist he talked about social security being, basically, as far as he was concerned, an impossible government program, to finance and to continue. Now that he`s a Republican candidate for Senate. He seems to be saying, oh now he wants to save Social Security, but he was part of a party, no matter what are you saying today, that has actively tried to cut the cost of living increase that everyone got and Social Security this year, the highest one from the government decades, because inflation is high.\par \par \uc2 And he`s joining a party for many of the senators already in place there, who remain in place are trying to basically repeal Social Security and to make it a program that gets funded, or doesn`t get funded, as the case may be, from year to year.\par \par \uc2 RYAN: Well, this is a huge issue here in Ohio. There`s no question about it, and all I will tell people in Ohio is this. And he told us they were going to overturn Roe v. Wade. They told us. We didn`t believe them.\par \par \uc2 Now they`re telling us they want to get rid of Social Security. They want to vote on it every five years, they want to privatize it. They want to privatize Medicare, we need to believe them.\par \par \uc2 That means that we need to fight this crew, as hard as we possibly can, and we need to make sure that we protect the retirement of our seniors, and the health care for seniors.\par \par \uc2 [22:15:04]\par \par \uc2 And that`s it, that`s the election, economic issues in Ohio, in rural areas. I mean, Social Security is the backbone of rural Ohio, and rural America, and we can`t let it get privatized.\par \par \uc2 And JD Vance doesn`t -- he does not care about the future of rural Ohio. So we have to continue to fight him.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: Congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , with his closing argument on tonight`s last word, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 RYAN: We`re going to bring it home, Lawrence.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: Gotcha.\par \par \uc2 RYAN: We`re going to bring home.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: Thank you very much. Really appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 RYAN: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 And coming up, Arizona Senator Mark Kelly will join us, on the final night of his reelection campaign. That`s next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [22:20:24]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 OBAMA: To say Mark Kelly is not a normal politician, is an understatement. Here is a guy, decorated, naval, aviator, you know and I had a "Top Gun" movie? All those people in the movie, those were actors, he is actually a top gun.\par \par \uc2 I like another legendary senator from Arizona. Mark has an independent streak. He knows how to work with anybody to get things done. Whether it`s putting