ponent on so many issues could not be more dramatic. You know, he has said that he wants to privatize Social Security, and he says that he wants a national abortion ban that`s so strict that even when a woman is raped she wouldn`t be able to make this decision. He says our military is totally incompetent.\par \par \uc2 So, in 12 days, Arizona has a choice. It is going to be a close election, and I have a go a great team that are working incredibly hard.\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: What do you say to the retiree committee in Arizona depending on their Social Security checks? They are not just depending on their current Social Security checks, they are depending on the increase, as they have this year, because of the cost of living increase that has been delivered to them.\par \par \uc2 That is something that Republicans have always opposed. They have always been trying to reduce, or eliminate the cost of living increase, and then many of them want to go beyond that and eliminate Social Security. What do you say to them about assuring them that that Social Security will be there for them?\par \par \uc2 KELLY: Well, what I tell them is that if I am reelected, I will fight for their Social Security, and their Medicare. And work to bring down the price of prescription drugs for seniors, which we did. And I was involved in negotiating that deal that is from out of pocket expenses, my opponent is against that.\par \par \uc2 He -- you know, where I stood up to big pharma, he stands with big pharma. So on all of these issues, you know, we could not be more different. We have a choice to make. We are really concerned about his views, about the military saying that we have not been a just war since before World War II.\par \par \uc2 This is an important election. And I think democracy is on the ballot here. We have got 12 days, I think we can get across the finish line successfully, but this is going to be a close race.\par \par \uc2 So, for folks out there that are watching, if 