bility?\par \par \uc2 STRAIN: Well, I think it -- I think it would be -- it would be terrible, reckless, irresponsible. It could -- it could be, you know, a catastrophe depending on how long the standoff lasted, depending on whether or not the global investors actually thought there was a risk that the United States wouldn`t pay its bills. But the best-case scenario is reckless, irresponsible damage and increases in borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: All right, \uc2 Michael Strain\uc2 , good to have you here. I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 STRAIN: Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Still to come, mass confusion in what should be a safe Democratic House seat. The retiring Democrat has to keep reminding constituents he`s not seeking another term because the Republican running to replace him has the exact same name. The tale to Mike Doyles next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [20:45:00]\par \par \uc2 HAYES: We`re under two weeks until the Midterm Elections, which of course we will be covering here in this studio on election night. Democrats hold the slim advantage to retain control of the Senate. Republicans favored to take back the House. But who knows? Neck and neck in a lot of races, neither party can afford to take any race for granted.\par \par \uc2 But one of the Democrats should be feeling pretty confident about is in Pennsylvania is newly redrawn 12th district. This is a blue area of Western Pennsylvania, includes the city of Pittsburgh and a good chunk of Allegheny County where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won by 20 points. Now, the Democratic nominee in the seat is Summer Lee. She`s a member of the Pennsylvania House. She should have a clear path to victory since this is essentially the seat that retiring Democratic Congressman Mike Doyle held for more than 25 years.\par \par \uc2 There`s just one small problem. Summer Lee is running to replace Mike Doyle against Mike Doyle.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Co