u look in the eyes of the people of the state of Florida and say to them, if you`re reelected, you will serve a full four- year term as governor, yes or no. Yes or no, Ron. Will you serve a full four-year term if you`re reelected governor of Florida? It`s not a tough question. It`s a fair question. He won`t tell you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Joining me now is \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , the Democratic candidate for governor of Florida. Mr. Crist, the governor seemed a little confused by that question because I think we all know what he wants to do should he win reelection here. He did not ultimately pledge he would serve a four-year term if I`m not mistaken.\par \par \uc2 CRIST: You are absolutely correct, Chris. And, you know, the sad part about that is Florida deserves better than that. I mean, this is a special state, a great place. And if somebody is going to run for governor of it, they ought to at least be willing to serve the term if the people are kind enough to elect you.\par \par \uc2 I if elected, will serve the full four-year term. That`s why I hope people will vote for our campaign. You know, I think it`s important that we have a governor who understands a woman`s right to choose is very important and respects it. DeSantis just signed a bill that said that there will be no right to choose in Florida, and not even exceptions for rape or incest. It`s unconscionable. Chris.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: The bill he signed, which there was a bit of exchange about this evening was, I believe, a 15-week ban which of course would be unconstitutional under Roe. It`s only possible under the new Dobbs ruling. Do you think that`s a popular position? I think Republicans tend to think like, oh, that`s the sort of in-between compromise position. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 [20:55:18]\par \par \uc2 CRIST: It is outrageously unpopular. And the truth of the matter is, the governor has always -- already indicated he wants to take it further. He wants 