wn almost 24 percent from this time last year. Doesn`t help that mortgage rates have skyrocketed.\par \par \uc2 The average for a 30-year fixed mortgage is now more than seven percent. And that`s more than double where it was at the beginning of the year. He was once known as one of the most powerful figures in the Trump White House. Now he`s headed for prison, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  sentencing and what it means for others who defy congressional subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 Plus, President Biden is on the move to Delaware where he will address student debt relief later today. The Supreme Court Justice that kept that plan in play might surprise you. And children`s hospitals are overwhelmed. The respiratory illness now spreading like wildfire, and how to stop it. You`re watching CHRIS JANSING REPORTS only on MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:21:07]\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Former Trump adviser \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  has been sentenced to prison and in the complex legal tentacles stemming from January 6 and the big lie. It`s one example of this. If you decide to ignore a subpoena, you`ll probably have to pay a price. Here`s a seemingly upbeat Bannon going into court. And then after being sentenced to four months in prison for refusing to comply with a January 6 committee`s subpoena. He was defiant.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 STEVE BANNON\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE CHIEF STRATEGIST: The American people are weighing and measuring what went on with the Justice Department and will how they comported themselves. They`re weighing and measuring that right now and they will vote on November 8th. \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  will end up being the first attorney general that`s brought up on charges impeachment, and he will be removed from office. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANSING: But it seems the judge is sending a very different message not just to Bannon but perhaps to the likes of \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc