y to lie to DOJ and try to hang on to these documents, long after he knew that they needed to go back. Of course, the evidence suggests he knew that from the get go. But now we`re learning that this is the sort of information that could really compromise national security and relationship with other nations if it fell into the wrong hands.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Meanwhile, Nick, were mentioned -- and we mentioned this, that we`re still waiting for the January 6 Committee to issue that subpoena to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Do we have any inkling why it`s taking so long?\par \par \uc2 CONFESSORE: Well, look, it`s a big decision. But he is the final piece of that puzzle. We have now heard over the past few months, a lot of testimony that points to his state of mind, the knowledge he had on that day. He was aware that the scheme to replace the electors was illegal and had no foundation. He was aware of the violence being perpetrated by his supporters. He was aware of a lot of things.\par \par \uc2 We haven`t heard from him. I`m not sure we need to hear from him in order to establish what happened that day, but certainly would give the committee and any future law enforcement effort here a chance to test what he says against the other evidence. It`s just basic. So I think they proceeded -- as you would imagine that they`re going to do him last. So that`s why it`s taking so long. I think,\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Nick, Joyce, Ken, good to have all of you here today. Have a great weekend. Meantime, Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  is allowing President Biden`s federal student loan forgiveness program to go forward. She rejected a request from a Wisconsin taxpayers group to block it. Without referring the matter to the other justices that is typically a signal she thinks the case was not on solid legal ground.\par \par \uc2 It was we should note part of a one-two punch in favor of the Biden administration. A federal judge also rejected a case against student loan forgiveness brought by six Republican-led states.\par \par \uc2 Actor Kevin Spacey was found not liable of sexual abuse by Manhattan jury and a high-profile civil case that could have implications for the future of legal cases surrounding the MeToo movement. Actor Anthony Rapp sued Spacey for battery, alleging the Oscar winner made sexual advances including laying on top of him at a party in 1986 when Rapp was just 14. Spacey`s defense team argued the allegations "never occurred at a party that was never held."\par \par \uc2 And new evidence Iran is helping Russia attack Ukraine on the ground. The potential global Fallout and what it means for the ongoing war in Ukraine. I`ll ask a former White House and state department official next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:33:35]\par \par \uc2 JANSING: New video from Russia shows a rare visit from \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to a base outside Moscow. It was aired on Russian state TV. He fired a sniper rifle and visited troops trying to send a message of strength as Russia`s battlefield losses in Ukraine continue to escalate. And today we know Iran did not just send Russian drones to use in Ukraine, they sent troops to help use those drones, too.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NED PRICE, STATE DEPARTMENT SPOKESPERSON: Credible information that points to the presence of Iranian drones inside Ukraine. The presence of Iranian trainers inside Ukraine operating in Crimea.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANSING: The new information comes right after Iran`s \uc2 U.N\uc2 . representative denied sending those drones at all. Meantime, Ukraine`s citizens continue to show extraordinary resilience after those Iranian drones destroyed a third of Ukraine`s power infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 Here is our Cal Perry talking with one 65-year-old woman.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAL PERRY, NBC NEWS CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): There could be no gas left, she says, no light, 