 And then when McCain shows Palin and of course, you know, he had initially thought about appointing Joe Lieberman as his vice president, as a dream ticket. And we just -- we talked about how different the direction of this country might have gone. But that was, I mean, it didn`t start with \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2 , start with Newt Gingrich. And I mean, a lot of other factors leading to where we are today in the Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 But the Palin decision was a real demarcation point, knock a lot of other dominoes that fell. And Tim makes a good point that I think David was kind of making too is that, you know, Palin could have been a campaign finance, Palin, but she was reacting to the crowds at the time. And she kind of fed off the anger and bitter resentment that so many people had. And there`s a lot of that out there today. And that`s the kind of thing is fueling a lot of the Republican candidacies, and the Marguerite Taylor Greenes that we see out there is that she`s seeing that I`m talking to the people in the district, and I hear it, I see it, and I`ve seen it this week. They`re mad and they see \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is somebody who will fight for them.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: All right, then David, Mark, thank you both for joining us. We will definitely see you again before the election.\par \par \uc2 MCKINNON: The number (INAUDIBLE) no doubt.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Coming up -- I mean when doesn`t he? Let`s be clear. I love when he qualifies it. I`m about to nerd out as though he doesn`t normally. Let`s be honest.\par \par \uc2 PLOUFFE: That`s very true.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Good to see you both. Coming up. Midterm politics in the President`s home state. I`m talking about PA. Who has got the voters fired up in the place that could decide the Senate when THE 11TH HOUR continues.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [23:37:50]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , U.S. PRESIDENT: I said when I ran: We`re going 