ut didn`t play football, so do you want me to listen to someone like that? I`m here to win a seat for the Georgia people. The Georgia people need a winner. They don`t need no one that we see going on right now. Georgia people need a winner.\par \par \uc2 (CHEERS AND APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Thanks, guys. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , repeatedly denying accusations that he paid for a woman to have an abortion.\par \par \uc2 Jonathan Lemire is back with me, we talked about this earlier, the playbook of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , deny, deny, deny, and simply claim I`m going to win this race.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN LEMIRE, POLITICO WHITE HOUSE BUREAU CHIEF: Yes, more of the same from \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  there. He didn`t have a lot to say. Very short answers. But what he did say was simply denials, that he didn`t pay for an abortion, that he wasn`t sure what this woman was talking about, he said that the harsh words from his former wife and his son, he didn`t know what that was, suggesting it was even a Democratic plot, and he repeated that he loved his family no matter what, and then he seemed to try to have a little fun there with a reporter about the upcoming debate with the incumbent Democratic Senator Raphael Warnock.\par \par \uc2 So, yes, not a particularly illuminating exchange there other than he`s going to give no ground. It is the Trump playbook. No explanations. No apologies. Don`t give an inch. Just stay high with the denials and hope that that`s enough for Republican voters there in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: And seeming to try, but not really having maybe any specific ammunition to criticize the lieutenant governor of Georgia, who said that the reason, and you heard the reporter say that, that the reason that, you know, he got the nomination, was because he scored a lot of touchdowns back in the `80s, and he seemed to be trying to imply somehow this is a guy who goes on TV a lot, is 