ump was inflating the values of his assets, and they wrote it down, deliberately tried to be more conservative.\par \par \uc2 But what are the fascinating things to me, and I`ve spent years studying \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 . And one of the fascinating things is reading kind of the details that are in this 200 plus page lawsuit that was filed yesterday is that there is a whole lot of granular detail that shows exactly what Trump was doing and Trump`s and Trump family members were doing as they tried to kind of turn one arm of \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  against another trying to turn one bank against another. And they were really using the representations that were in their financial statements to try to argue not only for more money, but also for lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 And it appears from what I`m seeing in these lawsuits, that they were very effective and that so even though Trump can argue that the banks should have known better, which is fair enough. What he can`t argue is that the banks didn`t pay attention to the financial information that he was putting forward because there`s clear records that they did.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: You just said Trump and Trump family members. OK, that means Don, Jr, Eric, Ivanka, who were officers in this company. So when Bill Barr goes on to why are they going after the kids. These aren`t kids. They themselves were personally involved in a number of these transactions.\par \par \uc2 ENRICH: Yes, I mean, the first other grownups, right. And so if kids makes it sounds like the -- project of DC she was the one who was having from what these documents in the lawsuit make it sound like was the one handling the lion`s share of the communication between the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  on the one hand and Rosemary Vrablic, who was the private banker at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  that was kind of the account manager.\par \par \uc2 She was directly involved. Her husband, \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  was the one who made the introduction from -- of Rosemary Vrablic to the Trump family. And Don, Jr. and Eric were also involved. So this is -- this was a family enterprise. There`s no question that the family was fully aware of what the patriarch was doing with kind of hyping and exaggerating his asset values in order to get more money for lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 And I think the question, I don`t know where legally that puts either Trump or his adult children. But there`s no doubt that they were all participating in this and doing everything they could to get as much money as possible, as cheaply as possible from \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: So no credible banks might want to lend to this guy going forward. But Trump is able to continue to fundraise. He was fundraising yesterday, off the suit from Tish James, despite the fact that there is another ongoing investigation into how he`s spending the money he`s raised from his pack.\par \par \uc2 Who are these donors? And at some point, are the donors like the banks like Dude, if you`re going to give this guy money, fire, beware, like he`s going to spend it wherever the heck he wants. You don`t care?\par \par \uc2 ENRICH: Yes, I mean, I think that`s a really good question. I don`t know the answer to that. And we`re seeing this play out in a bunch of different forums. Right. We learned that Trump has managed to repay most of what he owes \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  by getting some other kinds of third tier lenders to cough up hundreds of millions of dollars to lend to him.\par \par \uc2 We see what he`s doing with the fundraising appeals off of this lawsuit for his PACs that are already under investigation. We`re seeing this also with the social media company that he`s tried to get off the ground where the fundraising behind that is also under investigation by government agencies, including the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So basically, everywhere Trump is trying to raise money, there -- and this is a pattern that goes back decades. There has been kind of a trail of accusations and investigations and some pieces of wrongdoing left in his wake. And I think that spread continuing now.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: But at the same time, people keep writing him checks, like the Saudis. All of these golf tournaments at Trump clubs in the last year has given him a ton of money. So right now, behind the scenes, given the financial pressure he`s under, do you think we`re likely to see a fire sale of his assets? I mean, he still owns a lot.\par \par \uc2 ENRICH: Yes. I don`t, I mean, I don`t know. I think that he does own a lot. And I don`t think it would have to be a fire sale. I mean, he I think he surprised me by how much he got for the luxury hotel that he developed in Washington, DC. I think a lot of his properties while maybe his brand value has been diminished by how polarizing he is. I think that underlying assets probably have a lot of value.\par \par \uc2 And look, I mean, people have underestimated Trump and myself included in the financial space over and over and over again, and I`m going to try and be cautious not to do that again. And he certainly if he needed to drum up a bunch of cash to pay lawyers or to, you know, pay back loans, I think he`ll probably be able to do so at least for now.\par \par \uc2 [23:30:02]\par \par \uc2 But you know if all these legal crises that he`s facing really come to fruition and, you know, it`s possible he could be in much more severe financial straits,\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: But as of now he is not in financial straits, nor is his daughter and son in law reminder. \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  now running billions of dollars for MBS. David Enrich, thank you so much. I appreciate you joining us.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, drama surrounding the former guy is drowning out other important political news just six weeks before voters speak out. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  will not stop talking about his big plan to ban abortion nationwide. When THE